[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4187/images/16668/16668-1782428954-1893709378.gif[/img]

[size=6][color=#00ccff][b]AbsoluteHOTAS 4.0[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#ffaa00]Native HOTAS, HOSAS, flight-stick, throttle, pedal, and button-box support for Starfield.[/color][/b][/size]

[i]Direct hardware polling and analog ship-control injection. No vJoy, Joystick Gremlin, x360ce, Steam Input, or gamepad emulation. Plug in your hardware, bind it in-game, and fly.[/i][/center]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]Direct flight hardware support, now with profiles and macros[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Hot-Swappable Profiles:[/color][/b] Switch bindings, axes, tuning, aim behavior, and macros from a button or maintained selector position.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Macro Builder:[/color][/b] Create chords, taps, timed holds, ordered sequences, and turbo actions. Named ship actions follow your current Starfield keybinds.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Rebuilt Workbench:[/color][/b] Bind the essentials first, then open calibration, response tuning, profiles, macros, HOSAM/HOSAS modes, and specialist controls when needed.[/*]
[*][b]True Analog Flight Control:[/b] Direct authority over pitch, yaw, roll, strafe, throttle, and reverse without converting flight hardware into a virtual Xbox controller.[/*]
[*][b]Multi-Device Input:[/b] Mix sticks, throttles, pedals, button boxes, and custom DirectInput hardware in one setup.[/*]
[*][b]Advanced Throttle Support:[/b] Positional or self-centering throttle, reverse zones, detents, cruise controls, boost zones, and pilot turn assist.[/*]
[*][b]Independent Aim and HOSAM/HOSAS Modes:[/b] Separate steering from the weapon reticle, use aim-driven steering, or combine a left-hand stick with native mouse steering.[/*]
[*][b]Respects In-Game Rebinds:[/b] Ship buttons and macro actions reconcile against Starfield's current ControlMap instead of assuming vanilla keys.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffaa00][b]4.0.0-beta release track[/b][/color][/size][/center]

4.0.0 is an opt-in beta for the new configuration, profile, macro, and workbench systems. The established 3.0.2 file remains available as the stable fallback while 4.0 receives broader hardware and workflow testing.

[b]Please report reproducible crashes, stuck inputs, configuration loss, and core flight regressions first.[/b]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ff5555][b]Important 4.0 Upgrade Notice[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]4.0 is a fresh configuration baseline.[/b] Do not copy a 3.x AbsoluteHOTAS.ini into this release and do not import it as a 4.0 profile. Back up the old file for reference, install both new files, and rebuild the setup through the wizard.

After the first save, personal configuration is stored separately from shipped defaults. Full profile exports are the supported backup, sharing, and migration method going forward.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]Install and fly[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*]Starfield 1.16.242 or 1.16.244[/*]
[*]SFSE 0.2.20 or later[/*]
[*]No Starfield Address Library required[/*]
[/list]

[list=1]
[*]Install the archive normally with your mod manager.[/*]
[*]Launch Starfield through SFSE.[/*]
[*]Open the Starfield main or pause menu and press [color=#ffaa00][b]Ctrl+Alt+B[/b][/color].[/*]
[*]Bind your primary flight axes and desired ship buttons.[/*]
[*]Choose a convenient controller button for future wizard access, then click [b]Save & Close[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[i]For full mouse interaction, open the wizard from a Starfield menu. During gameplay the game retains its mouse lock; the wizard remains usable with standard keyboard navigation.[/i]

[line]

